  "answer_core": "Don’t commit this week to 15% equity, a board seat, or a CTO title. Those are irreversible moves before you know whether the partnership reduces or concentrates risk.\n\nUse Friday for a direct, structured, staged‑path offer. Make clear you’re open to significant upside for him, but only after evidence. Set a short, defined sprint that tests whether he can deliver the key platform work, whether that work matters for revenue, whether team stability improves, whether knowledge transfer happens, and whether his governance behavior fits what the company needs. Spell out what success in that window would unlock.\n\nThis avoids both a premature commitment and a vague delay. You give him a real path forward, tied to demonstrated impact rather than hypothetical valuation math.",
